{"step_index":74,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T15:31:44Z","content":"# Deployment & Audit Report: StreamWave Serverless Media Platform\n\nThe **StreamWave Serverless Media Platform** has been audited, fully tested, and prepared for zero-configuration deployment to **Vercel** as a non-commercial academic prototype on the Vercel Hobby plan.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Pre-Deployment Verification Checklist\n\n| Requirement | Status | Details |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Automated Tests** | **PASS (10/10)** | All API endpoints (`/api/health`, `/api/media`, `/api/media/1`, `POST /api/play-events`), query filtering, and 404/422 validation pass in `tests/test_api.py`. |\n| **FastAPI Entry Point** | **CONFIRMED** | [`app.py`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/app.py) exports `app = FastAPI(...)` at root level. |\n| **Python Version** | **CONFIRMED** | [`pyproject.toml`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/pyproject.toml) specifies `requires-python = \">=3.12, <3.13\"`. |\n| **Vercel Framework Detection** | **CONFIRMED** | Obsolete `@vercel/python` builders avoided. Native Vercel zero-config Python runtime enabled. |\n| **Secrets Protection** | **CONFIRMED** | [`.gitignore`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/.gitignore) excludes `.env`, `.env.local`, and token keys. |\n\n---\n\n### 2. Vercel Authentication & Deployment Authorization Steps\n\nTo complete the deployment to your Vercel account, follow these authorization steps:\n\n#### Option A: Direct Deployment via Vercel CLI\n1. Open your terminal in the project directory (`streamwave-serverless`).\n2. Run the Vercel login command:\n   ```bash\n   npx vercel login\n   ```\n   *Action Required*: Select your preferred login method (GitHub, GitLab, or Email) in the browser window that opens and authorize Vercel CLI access.\n3. Run the deployment command:\n   ```bash\n   npx vercel --prod\n   ```\n   - **Set up and deploy?**: `Y`\n   - **Which scope?**: Select your personal Vercel Hobby account scope.\n   - **Link to existing project?**: `N\n<truncated 2631 bytes>\nnd cause build errors on modern Vercel runtimes. | Removed legacy build definitions; relied on Vercel's native zero-config FastAPI detection via root `app.py`. |\n| **Static File Fallback in Serverless Environment** | Static files mounted at `/` could overshadow `/api` endpoints if registered in wrong order. | Explicitly registered all `/api/*` routes before `app.mount(\"/\", StaticFiles(...))` in [`app.py`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/app.py). |\n| **Read-Only Filesystem Constraint** | Serverless functions on Vercel use an ephemeral read-only filesystem where runtime file writing fails. | Structured `POST /api/play-events` to log events via standard `logger.info()` directly to Vercel runtime logs without filesystem writes. |\n\n---\n\n### 📷 Assignment Evidence Screenshot Checklist\n\nCapture the following numbered screenshots for your academic submission:\n\n1. **Screenshot 1: Local Pytest Execution**: Terminal output showing 10/10 tests passing in `tests/test_api.py`.\n2. **Screenshot 2: Production Web Interface (Desktop)**: Browser showing `https://<your-project-name>.vercel.app/` with the StreamWave hero section and dark graphite design.\n3. **Screenshot 3: Mobile Layout & Filters**: Browser Developer Tools in mobile responsive view (<768px width) demonstrating filtered media items (e.g. Type: Music).\n4. **Screenshot 4: Accessible Media Details Modal**: Open `<dialog>` modal showing media metadata for *Cook Off*.\n5. **Screenshot 5: HTML5 Audio Player & Network Tab**: DevTools **Network** tab showing `demo.wav` loading directly as a static asset alongside the active audio player bar.\n6. **Screenshot 6: OpenAPI Swagger Documentation**: Browser viewing `https://<your-project-name>.vercel.app/docs`.\n7. **Screenshot 7: Vercel Dashboard Deployment**: Overview page in Vercel Dashboard showing successful production deployment status.\n8. **Screenshot 8: Vercel Runtime Logs**: Log viewer in Vercel Dashboard confirming the structured JSON output from `POST /api/play-events`.","thinking":"**Reviewing Deployment Requirements**\n\nOkay, I'm now reviewing the specific steps needed to deploy the tested StreamWave FastAPI serverless application to Vercel, based on the approved FastAPI deployment method. I'm ensuring all automated tests pass first, then I'll verify that `app.py` is configured correctly, exporting the FastAPI app from a supported entry point. Finally, I'll confirm Python 3 compatibility.\n\n\n**Verifying Deployment Readiness**\n\nI'm now focusing on authenticating with Vercel for deployment, as direct CLI execution failed earlier. I must ensure I understand the authorization steps the user must take, especially if GitHub integration is required. The authorization step involves using `vercel login` or Git repository integration, not revealing credentials. I'm stopping to clarify the required authentication, before attempting deployment.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":75,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T15:32:17Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nUsing only the actual completed StreamWave project and verified Vercel deployment, prepare a concise academic implementation report.\nDo not invent URLs, screenshots, tests, configurations or results.\nInclude:\nTitle of the practical solution.\nPurpose of the implementation.\nJustification for selecting Vercel and FastAPI.\nFunctional requirements implemented.\nArchitecture and explanation of each component.\nDevelopment and deployment procedure.\nTesting performed with actual results.\nSecurity controls implemented.\nEvidence list with numbered screenshot placeholders.\nExplanation of how the prototype would integrate into the wider StreamWave platform.\nLimitations of the prototype.\nConclusion.\nClearly explain that:\nFastAPI executes as a Vercel serverless function.\nStatic media or Vercel Blob delivers sample media directly to users.\nPlayback events are written to runtime logs and are not presented as permanent database records.\nA production StreamWave platform would require authenticated users, persistent databases, private media delivery, transcoding, digital-rights controls and more extensive monitoring.\nThe Hobby deployment is a non-commercial academic prototype.\nUse verifiable official sources and Harvard-style in-text citations. Include a complete reference list with publication or last-updated dates. Prefer:\n[https://vercel.com/docs/frameworks/backend/fastapi](https://vercel.com/docs/frameworks/backend/fastapi)\n[https://vercel.com/docs/functions/runtimes/python](https://vercel.com/docs/functions/runtimes/python)\n[https://vercel.com/docs/logs/runtime](https://vercel.com/docs/logs/runtime)\n[https://vercel.com/docs/vercel-blob](https://vercel.com/docs/vercel-blob)\n[https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/features/](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/features/)\nWrite approximately 1,200–1,500 words in formal academic language.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-08-25T17:32:17+02:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
