{"step_index":82,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T15:33:15Z","content":"Here are the exact **Windows Command Prompt (`cmd.exe`)** commands to set up, test, and run the project locally.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Open `cmd.exe` and Navigate to the Project Folder\n\n```cmd\ncd C:\\Users\\dell\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Create & Activate Virtual Environment\n\n```cmd\npython -m venv .venv\n.venv\\Scripts\\activate.bat\n```\n*(Your command prompt will now show `(.venv)` at the beginning of the line).*\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Install Dependencies\n\n```cmd\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Generate the Demonstration Audio File\n\n```cmd\npython scripts\\generate_demo_audio.py\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Run the Automated Unit Tests\n\n```cmd\npytest tests\\test_api.py -v\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 6: Start the Development Server\n\n```cmd\nuvicorn app:app --reload --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000\n```\n\nOnce running, open your web browser at:\n- **Web App**: `http://127.0.0.1:8000`\n- **Swagger Docs**: `http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs`\n\n---\n\n### Optional: Set Vercel Blob Environment Variable in CMD\n\nTo test the Vercel Blob URL override in Windows `cmd.exe`:\n\n```cmd\nset STREAMWAVE_BLOB_URL=https://public.blob.vercel-storage.com/demo.wav\nuvicorn app:app --reload\n```"}
