{"step_index":95,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T15:45:34Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nImprove the existing StreamWave Entertainment interface without rebuilding the project or changing its working FastAPI backend.\r\n\r\nFirst inspect the current files and understand how the interface, catalogue API, filtering, media details, playback and event logging work. Preserve all existing API endpoints, data structures, tests, Vercel configuration and working functionality.\r\n\r\nMake only the following interface improvements:\r\n\r\n1. PLAYBACK LABELS\r\n\r\n* Movie cards must display “Watch Preview”.\r\n* Music cards must display “Play Sample”.\r\n* The featured-content button must use the correct label according to its media type.\r\n* Do not use “Play Demo” on every card.\r\n* If multiple catalogue items use the same generated demonstration file, show a discreet “Technical sample” label and do not imply that copyrighted content is being streamed.\r\n\r\n2. HEADER\r\n\r\n* Reduce the visual size of the “Serverless Demonstration” badge.\r\n* Keep it visible because it is important for the academic assessment.\r\n* Replace the primary “API Docs” navigation link with a smaller “Developer” link or menu that opens `/docs`.\r\n* Maintain a clean, balanced desktop header.\r\n* Ensure the header works properly on tablets and mobile phones.\r\n\r\n3. MEDIA CARDS\r\n\r\n* Allow long titles to occupy a maximum of two lines instead of cutting them off too early.\r\n* Add a tooltip or title attribute containing the complete title.\r\n* Make the cover image and title clickable.\r\n* Add subtle professional hover and keyboard-focus states.\r\n* Keep one clear primary playback button and one secondary details button.\r\n* Maintain equal card heights within each row.\r\n* Do not add excessive rounded corners, glass effects, glowing borders or unnecessary gradients.\r\n\r\n4. AUDIO PLAYER\r\n\r\n* Ensure the fixed bottom player never covers catalogue cards or footer content.\r\n* Add sufficient bottom padding to the page.\r\n* Display the selected track’s title, artist and cover thumbnail.\r\n* Show a helpful “Select a track to play” state befo\n<truncated 574 bytes>\n\n6. ACCESSIBILITY\r\n\r\n* Add visible `:focus-visible` indicators.\r\n* Ensure buttons have meaningful accessible names.\r\n* Ensure modal focus is managed correctly.\r\n* Allow the details modal to close using Escape.\r\n* Ensure text has sufficient contrast against the dark background.\r\n* Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.\r\n* Use semantic HTML headings, navigation, buttons and labels.\r\n\r\n7. CONTENT AND ACADEMIC CLARITY\r\n\r\n* Add a small footer statement explaining that the application is a non-commercial academic serverless prototype.\r\n* State that displayed media metadata and generated samples are used for demonstration.\r\n* Do not add or download copyrighted music, film clips or images.\r\n* Do not invent streaming rights or partnerships.\r\n\r\n8. VISUAL STYLE\r\n\r\n* Preserve the dark graphite, white and restrained red StreamWave colour scheme.\r\n* Maintain the current Zimbabwean entertainment focus.\r\n* Use strong typography, consistent spacing and clean rectangular cards.\r\n* Make the result look like a credible entertainment platform rather than a generic AI-generated dashboard.\r\n* Do not replace the interface with a template or introduce a frontend framework.\r\n\r\n9. VERIFICATION\r\n\r\n* Test search, media-type filtering, genre filtering, details modal, audio playback and navigation.\r\n* Confirm that the correct button label is generated for each media type.\r\n* Test desktop, tablet and mobile layouts.\r\n* Run all existing automated tests.\r\n* Fix any regression introduced by the interface changes.\r\n* Do not report success unless the tests and manual checks have actually been completed.\r\n\r\nWhen finished, provide:\r\n\r\n1. The files changed.\r\n2. A concise explanation of each improvement